   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 2. NGO State Watch</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support evidence-based policy discussions and contribute to the continued strengthening of transparency, accountability, and integrity in Ukraine&#x2019;s defence procurement system.
The project tasks are:
1) Monitoring of defence procurement. Conduct systematic monitoring of non-lethal centralised defence procurement and prepare monthly analytical reports identifying procurement inefficiencies, potential irregularities, and integrity risks.
2) Annual procurement assessment. Prepare a comprehensive assessment of the 2025 non-lethal centralised procurement cycle conducted by the State Logistics Operator (DOT), evaluating procurement efficiency, transparency safeguards, and accountability mechanisms.
3)  Development of policy recommendations. Produce analytical policy briefs based on monitoring findings, providing practical recommendations to improve procurement procedures and integrity safeguards.
4)  Stakeholder dialogue. Organise policy discussions with government institutions, oversight bodies, and civil society representatives to discuss findings and jointly develop actionable recommendations.
5) Documentation of good practices. Prepare a brief identifying effective integrity safeguards and practices in defence procurement under wartime conditions.
The objective of the project &#x201c;Enhancing Integrity in Defence Procurement Through Civilian Oversight&#x201d; is to reduce corruption risks in Ukraine&#x2019;s defence procurement through strengthened civilian oversight, enhanced integrity safeguards, and evidence-based policy reform, contributing to increased public trust in defence sector governance.</narrative>
  </description>
